{
  "abstract": "A connected non-bipartite graph on 24 vertices has radius 10 and floods in three synchronous rounds from four sources, so its optimal four-source flooding time t satisfies 4t ≤ 12 < 13. Repeating the gadget gives a counterexample to Turau's Section 8 inequality for every source count k ≥ 4, with exact radius floor(5k/2) and optimal k-source flooding time at most 3.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Jaime Nistal"
    }
  ],
